ce","rust","zig"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/lh1j0e","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/lh1j0e/shlemiel_painter_is_back_how_zig_s_libc"},{"short_id":"bqllfe","created_at":"2026-11-04T08:58:11.018-06:00","title":"Your Cryptography Conspiracy Theory Is Wrong","url":"https://soatok.blog/2026/10/29/your-cryptography-conspiracy-theory-is-wrong/","score":39,"flags":1,"comment_count":2,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"fanf","user_is_author":false,"tags":["cryptography"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/bqllfe","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/bqllfe/your_cryptography_conspiracy_theory_is"},{"short_id":"5xljpx","created_at":"2026-11-04T08:50:34.331-06:00","title":"Lorem Ipsum Dot Gov Dot UK","url":"https://shkspr.mobi/blog/2026/11/lorem-ipsum-dot-gov-dot-uk/","score":11,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"aggsol","user_is_author":false,"tags":["testing","web"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/5xljpx","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/5xljpx/lorem_ipsum_dot_gov_dot_uk"},{"short_id":"mvjqj0","created_at":"2026-11-04T08:13:15.593-06:00","title":"Chatastrophe: Your server's disasters, delivered by Nostr DM","url":"","score":-4,"flags":5,"comment_count":0,"description":"\u003cp\u003eI built a tool that is making my life a little easier: Chatastrophe\n\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/dtonon/chatastrophe\" rel=\"ugc\"\u003ehttps://github.com/dtonon/chatastrophe\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe idea is simple, a small bash check that runs on a server every 10 minutes and sends a Nostr DM (NIP-17) when something goes wrong:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDisk usage above a threshold;\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAvailable RAM below a threshold, or swap usage above one;\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eProcesses killed by the out-of-memory killer since the previous run;\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eA file (for example a database) larger than a set size;\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eA systemd unit not active, or restarted too many times in the last hour;\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can also ping your bot and ask for a server status report.\nFinally, with some trepidation, you can blindly restart one of the configured systemd units!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSince so many people now have their own server, even if it's just to run a small website or a personal Nostr relay, I invite you to give it a try. Any feedback is welcome :)\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"I built a tool that is making my life a little easier: Chatastrophe\r\nhttps://github.com/dtonon/chatastrophe\r\n\r\nThe idea is simple, a small bash check that runs on a server every 10 minutes and sends a Nostr DM (NIP-17) when something goes wrong:\r\n\r\n- Disk usage above a threshold;\r\n- Available RAM below a threshold, or swap usage above one;\r\n- Processes killed by the out-of-memory killer since the previous run;\r\n- A file (for example a database) larger than a set size;\r\n- A systemd unit not active, or restarted too many times in the last hour;\r\n\r\nYou can also ping your bot and ask for a server status report.\r\nFinally, with some trepidation, you can blindly restart one of the configured systemd units!\r\n\r\nSince so many people now have their own server, even if it's just to run a small website or a personal Nostr relay, I invite you to give it a try. Any feedback is welcome :)","submitter_user":"daniele","user_is_author":true,"tags":["devops","linux","release","show","systemd"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/mvjqj0","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/mvjqj0/chatastrophe_your_server_s_disasters"},{"short_id":"ecrqpy","created_at":"2026-11-04T08:05:16.766-06:00","title":"How to speed up the Rust compiler in November 2026","url":"https://nnethercote.github.io/2026/11/04/how-to-speed-up-the-rust-compiler-in-november-2026.html","score":25,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitte